other hand, speculation that there has,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:24.640
without a doubt, intelligence experts are paid&nbsp;
to provide all options to elected officials&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:31.840
and that it would be unusual that the question of&nbsp;
could Putin be assassinated, would not have come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:36.160
up. Not that anyone's planning to do it, but that&nbsp;
this is what intelligence people are paid to do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:42.080
provide every option. Can you weigh in&nbsp;
at all on either of those two things?&nbsp;

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:46.320
Speaker 4: I certainly am not privy to any&nbsp;
knowledge that is an out there in the American&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:53.840
public. So I guess first I would just say that it&nbsp;
would be absolutely wrong. It is not. The United&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:59.280
States policy should not be the United States&nbsp;
policy to try to assassinate a sitting head of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:07.040
state of another country. And I would vigorously&nbsp;
oppose something like that. And it's nothing that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:13.680
I have heard of being planned. And I don't think&nbsp;
in any way is the policy of this administration.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:19.440
The second point about Putin's health, I&nbsp;
mean, I've read about the same speculation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:28.000
